  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Wednesday...\n\nA cold front has moved through the region overnight, creating \nslightly cooler conditions for today. As higher pressures fill in,\nwindy conditions are expected to persist through the day across\neastern MT. There is still about a 60-80% chance for gusts to 50\nmph along the MT/Dakotas border. Through Saturday, higher heights\nand ridging will move in, creating warm and dry conditions with \nhigh temperatures in the upper 60s and 70s. With a tighter \ngradient aloft and mild 700 mb winds, breezy conditions will be in\nplace for areas south of Billings to the WY border including the\nFort Smith area. The Livingston/Big Timber corridor will also be\nwindy late Friday evening through Saturday afternoon. A dry \nbackdoor front is expected to move through Saturday evening and \novernight, cooling temperatures back to near average, in the upper\n50s to low 60s. Conditions will remain mild Monday into Tuesday \nas westerly flow transitions southwesterly. Depending on the track\nof the low off the west coast middle of next week, the region \ncould get into a pattern of daily afternoon showers and a few \nthunderstorms. Currently there are low chances for precipitation \nacross south- central MT Tuesday into Wednesday. There is still \nuncertainty at this time, so watch the forecast to see how this \nsystem progresses. TS",
